# DRAFT (Story 14.4): the tavern's disturbances. Raphael to rewrite. The hall's director opens a title by the event's
# type and truth (data/disturbances/disturbances.json); a reply records the player's answer with bridge.choose(id) and the
# outcome follows when the box closes; a reply that chooses nothing (or Esc) leaves the visitor there for later. Game
# state only through `bridge` (scripts/dialogue/dialogue_bridge.gd).

~ thief_guilty
Stranger: Evening. Just warming my hands.
Stranger: This purse? Found it under a table. Lucky night.
- Throw him out.
	do bridge.choose("eject")
	Stranger: All right, all right. No need to shove.
- Leave him be.
	do bridge.choose("let_be")
	Stranger: Kind of you. Very kind.
- (Walk away.)
=> END

~ thief_innocent
Stranger: Evening. I'm waiting for my brother. He said the guild's tavern, by the fire.
Stranger: He's late. He's always late.
- Throw him out.
	do bridge.choose("eject")
	Stranger: I've done nothing! ... Fine. Tell him I waited.
- Leave him be.
	do bridge.choose("let_be")
	Stranger: Thank you. I'll keep out of the way.
- (Walk away.)
=> END

~ rowdy_drunk
Drunk: Another round! The house is buying! Isn't it?
Drunk: Nobody sings anymore. Why does nobody sing?
- Show him the door.
	do bridge.choose("eject")
	Drunk: Fine. Fine! I know when I'm not loved.
- Let him sing.
	do bridge.choose("let_be")
	Drunk: That's the spirit!
- (Walk away.)
=> END

~ grieving_family
if bridge.disturbance_subject != ""
	Mourner: {{bridge.disturbance_subject}} rode out with your guild. They told me there's nothing to bury.
Mourner: I'm not here to shout. I wanted to see the place they chose.
- Give her some coin.
	do bridge.choose("pay")
	Mourner: It won't fix anything. Thank you all the same.
- Tell her about them.
	do bridge.choose("talk")
	Mourner: That sounds like them. Yes.
- Ask her to leave.
	do bridge.choose("send_away")
	Mourner: I see. I'll go.
- (Walk away.)
=> END

~ rival_guild_rep
Rival: Nice little place. The Silver Compass sends its regards.
Rival: We're taking contracts on the east road now. Thought you'd want to hear it from us.
- Wish him luck.
	do bridge.choose("courteous")
	Rival: Generous. We'll see how long that lasts.
- Buy him a drink.
	do bridge.choose("drink")
	Rival: Now that's how guilds should talk.
- Tell him to leave.
	do bridge.choose("eject")
	Rival: Touchy. I'll tell them you said hello.
- (Walk away.)
=> END
